From 9ef2da302ceaaa71f5056a8f564313e7759f48ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:56:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bugfix: harden the legacy age arithmetic dependency

Address RUSTSEC-2026-0387 in the age0.12.1 dependency chain using the independently reviewed crypto-bigint0.5.5 backport. Reconstruct and compare the complete vendor source, then verify actual locked resolution before the strict advisory audit. Keep other registry versions optional while validating them when present.

The frozen18-path library patch remains daab4a04c34beea7f417fae1b348ada597221bed826c9fc0b6c0cdcef00d0002. All28 guard regressions and the full strict audit pass on the release queue. Clean-base standalone packaging separately includes its minimal ctutils0.4.5 update; this queue-context artifact uses the existing0.4.5 lock entry. Bazel consumer and final platform acceptance remain required.
